---
components: ["ToastNotification", "NotificationActionButton"]
description: Toast notifications are non-modal, time-based messages that appear briefly and dismiss automatically. They support multiple types and custom content.
---

<script>
  import { NotificationActionButton, ToastNotification } from "carbon-components-svelte";
</script>

## Basic

Display a basic error notification with title, subtitle, and timestamp by default. See [detailed usage](https://carbondesignsystem.com/components/notification/usage) and the related [InlineNotification](InlineNotification). For an imperative API to manage multiple toasts with automatic queue management, see [NotificationQueue](NotificationQueue).

<ToastNotification titleText="Session expired" subtitleText="Your session has ended. Please sign in again to continue." captionText="{new Date().toLocaleString()}" />

## Reusable

Control notification visibility by binding to `open` to show, hide, and reuse the same component with different messages. Open defaults to true.

<FileSource src="/framed/ToastNotification/ToastNotificationReusable" />

## Autoclose

Automatically close the notification after a specified duration (in milliseconds) with `timeout`. Set `pauseOnHover` to pause the timeout while the pointer is over the toast or while focus is inside it, so users can finish reading (opt-in).

A toast with an action, or an actionable toast, ignores `timeout`. It stays
open until users act on it or close it, so the action never disappears
before they reach it.

<FileSource src="/framed/ToastNotification/ToastNotificationTimeout" />

## Actions

Add an action, such as a retry, in the `actions` snippet. A
`NotificationActionButton` there renders as a small tertiary button
under the text, in colors that read on every kind. The toast's title
describes the button for screen readers, with no extra setup.

<ToastNotification kind="error" titleText="Upload failed" subtitleText="The connection timed out before quarterly-report.pdf finished." captionText="{new Date().toLocaleString()}">
  {#snippet actions()}
    <NotificationActionButton>Retry</NotificationActionButton>
  {/snippet}
</ToastNotification>
<ToastNotification lowContrast kind="error" titleText="Upload failed" subtitleText="The connection timed out before quarterly-report.pdf finished." captionText="{new Date().toLocaleString()}">
  {#snippet actions()}
    <NotificationActionButton>Retry</NotificationActionButton>
  {/snippet}
</ToastNotification>

## Actionable

Set `actionable` to `true` when users must reach an action in the
toast, such as a retry after a failed upload. Place the action in the
`actions` snippet. The toast becomes an `alertdialog` named by its title and
described by its subtitle. When it opens, focus moves to the first
action, or to the close button if there is no action. Tab stays inside
the toast, and <DocKbd label="Escape" /> closes it. Focus then returns
to where it was before, such as the button that opened it.

Set `focusOnOpen` to `false` to leave focus in place, or
`closeOnEscape` to `false` to keep it open on <DocKbd label="Escape" />.
If the close button is also hidden, Tab can leave the toast, so
keyboard users are never trapped. The toast ignores `timeout`, so it
cannot close before users act.
[NotificationQueue](NotificationQueue) accepts the same options.

<FileSource src="/framed/ToastNotification/ToastNotificationActionable" />

## Full width

Span the full container width with `fullWidth`.

<ToastNotification fullWidth titleText="Session expired" subtitleText="Your session has ended. Please sign in again to continue." captionText="{new Date().toLocaleString()}" />

## Title, subtitle, caption

All three are optional and can be customized with slots.

### Optional

Title, subtitle, and caption each render only when provided.

<ToastNotification subtitleText="Your session has ended. Please sign in again to continue." />
<ToastNotification titleText="Session expired" subtitleText="Your session has ended. Please sign in again to continue." />
<ToastNotification subtitleText="Your session has ended. Please sign in again to continue." captionText="{new Date().toLocaleString()}" />
<ToastNotification titleText="Export complete" captionText="{new Date().toLocaleString()}" />

### Custom (slots)

Customize the notification content using slots for more flexibility.

<ToastNotification>
  {#snippet titleText()}<strong>Session expired: </strong>{/snippet}
  {#snippet subtitleText()}<strong>Your session has ended. Please sign in again to continue.</strong>{/snippet}
  {#snippet captionText()}<strong>{new Date().toLocaleString()}</strong>{/snippet}
</ToastNotification>

## Close button

Hide the close button or customize its behavior and label.

### Hidden

Create a persistent notification by hiding the close button.

<ToastNotification hideCloseButton kind="warning" titleText="Elevated error rate" subtitleText="The payments service is experiencing elevated error rates. This message will remain until resolved." captionText="{new Date().toLocaleString()}" />

### Translated label

Translate the close button label via `closeButtonDescription`.

<ToastNotification
  titleText="会话已过期"
  subtitleText="您的会话已过期,请重新登录以继续。"
  closeButtonDescription="关闭通知"
/>

### Prevent default

`onopenchange` is called with `{ open: false, trigger }` when the user closes
the notification: `"close-button"`, `"escape-key"` on an actionable
notification, or `"timeout"` when `timeout` runs out. Call `preventDefault()`
on it to keep the notification open. It isn't called when `open` is set from
outside.

<ToastNotification titleText="Session expired" subtitleText="Your session has ended. Please sign in again to continue." captionText="{new Date().toLocaleString()}" onopenchange={(e) => {
  e.preventDefault();
  // custom close logic (e.g., transitions)
}} />

## ARIA role

Screen readers announce a notification when it appears. The default,
`role="status"`, waits until the user pauses. Use it for most messages,
such as a finished export.

Set `role="alert"` for an urgent error that needs action now, such as a
failed payment. An alert interrupts whatever the screen reader is
reading, so keep it rare. Set `role="log"` for a running log of
messages.

<ToastNotification kind="success" titleText="Export complete" subtitleText="Your report has been exported and is ready for download." captionText="{new Date().toLocaleString()}" />
<ToastNotification role="alert" kind="error" titleText="Payment failed" subtitleText="Update your card to keep the workspace active." captionText="{new Date().toLocaleString()}" />

## Status icon label

The status icon has a label for screen readers, such as "Warning" for
the warning kinds. Translate it with `statusIconDescription`.

<ToastNotification
  kind="warning"
  titleText="Maintenance planifiée"
  subtitleText="La facturation est en lecture seule samedi de 02:00 à 04:00 UTC."
  statusIconDescription="Avertissement"
  closeButtonDescription="Fermer la notification"
/>

## Variants

The component supports different notification types.

### High contrast

<ToastNotification kind="error" titleText="Session expired" subtitleText="Your session has ended. Please sign in again to continue." captionText="{new Date().toLocaleString()}" />
<ToastNotification kind="info" titleText="Update available" subtitleText="A new version of the admin console is ready to install." captionText="{new Date().toLocaleString()}"  />
<ToastNotification kind="info-square" titleText="Update available" subtitleText="A new version of the admin console is ready to install." captionText="{new Date().toLocaleString()}" />
<ToastNotification kind="success" titleText="Export complete" subtitleText="Your report has been exported and is ready for download." captionText="{new Date().toLocaleString()}" />
<ToastNotification kind="warning" titleText="Disk space low" subtitleText="The application server has less than 10% of disk space remaining." captionText="{new Date().toLocaleString()}" />
<ToastNotification kind="warning-alt" titleText="Disk space low" subtitleText="The application server has less than 10% of disk space remaining." captionText="{new Date().toLocaleString()}" />

### Low contrast

Use low contrast variants for less prominent notifications.

<ToastNotification lowContrast kind="error" titleText="Session expired" subtitleText="Your session has ended. Please sign in again to continue." captionText="{new Date().toLocaleString()}" />
<ToastNotification lowContrast kind="info" titleText="Update available" subtitleText="A new version of the admin console is ready to install." captionText="{new Date().toLocaleString()}" />
<ToastNotification lowContrast kind="info-square" titleText="Update available" subtitleText="A new version of the admin console is ready to install." captionText="{new Date().toLocaleString()}" />
<ToastNotification lowContrast kind="success" titleText="Export complete" subtitleText="Your report has been exported and is ready for download." captionText="{new Date().toLocaleString()}" />
<ToastNotification lowContrast kind="warning" titleText="Disk space low" subtitleText="The application server has less than 10% of disk space remaining." captionText="{new Date().toLocaleString()}" />
<ToastNotification lowContrast kind="warning-alt" titleText="Disk space low" subtitleText="The application server has less than 10% of disk space remaining." captionText="{new Date().toLocaleString()}" />
